Gate: tsc 0; 2336 tests; build OK. Ephemerals were removed in src/tools/brain (plan + brief), src/service/brainContract, src/types, src/service/install/initContent, src/tools/upgrade/brainCategory and src.

The aide-maintainer prose now names aide_cleanup's `path` parameter; all 6 maintainers had guessed a wrong name first.

versions.json lists 43 artifacts because the new skill has no git history yet. After commit, a rebuild gives 44.

Feature `versions-manifest-release-hygiene` (In Review) is built, has passed QA, and is committed on main. It is not published; latest release is still v0.10.4.

What landed:

- New build-time helper assertFullClone (src/tools/upgrade/buildVersionsMeta/assertFullClone) with 5 tests. scripts/build-versions.ts exits 1 on a shallow or unknown-depth clone.
- `fetch-depth: 0` in publish.yml and ci.yml.
- package.json: a `clean` script (node fs.rmSync) runs first in `build`. prepublishOnly is `npm run build`. files gets "!.aide/versions.json".
- .aide/versions.json removed from git and gitignored.

Gate: tsc 0; 2160 tests; the clean build removes stale dist files; dist/versions.json has 43 entries with 22 distinct sourceCommits and previousCommit on 41; a real depth-1 clone aborts the build; npm pack excludes .aide/versions.json even when present.

QA passed with no todo.aide (no retro). plan.aide was removed through aide_cleanup. With the stale host file gone, aide_info in this repo reports no outdated artifacts.

User impact (corrected with the user, 2026-10-10): the recurring 'outdated' prompt happened only in this repo. Its stale committed .aide/versions.json was never rewritten, because this repo is never upgraded onto itself. In host projects the prompt shows once per release and accepting the upgrade clears it. The depth-1 stamping only inflates that one prompt's count, all 43 instead of just the changed artifacts, so it is cosmetic. The in-repo fix is complete without a publish. The full-history manifest ships with the next release, whenever that is; it does not warrant a release on its own.

Previous releases: v0.10.4 (session.aide is the full session record), v0.10.3 (boot upgrade gate), v0.10.2 (content-free brain responses), v0.10.1 a broken tag; global install 0.10.4; aidemd.dev synced to 0.10.4 (site commit 160ad91).

