## Process discipline (permanent)

- One implementor per numbered plan step.
- Prose never goes through the pipeline — agent instructions, methodology docs, README and wording-only text changes are edited directly by the main agent; only behavior-changing code is pipelined (user, 2026-10-09).
- Pause for user approval before the build.
- Every /aide session checks the board at boot and keeps the feature's tasks and `## Kanban` links current.
- Record the work in session.aide in full (decision 23); stash into tasks alongside.
- Cleanup of plan/todo/brief goes through aide_cleanup via aide-maintainer.
- Release process (user, 2026-10-11), done by the agent every time it publishes: check `git status` (publish.mjs commits everything staged) → publish and confirm the Publish workflow and npm version → `npm i -g @aidemd-mcp/server@<version>` → run a headless `claude -p` session from inside the aidemd.dev checkout that applies the drifted package-owned upgrade categories through aide_upgrade (never mcp or brain), commits `chore(aide): sync methodology to <version>` and pushes to main (the push deploys via GitHub Pages) → confirm the deploy → update session.aide. Never hand-edit the site's files from this repo's session; the headless session in the site folder does the work through aide's own tools. If it reports brainMigration, tell the user (/aide:brain config needs their consent).
- Keep session.aide up to date as you work (decision 22).
